autoortho-scenery (flightwusel packages)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ZL=${ZL}
VARIANT=${VARIANT} (for X-Plane 12)
VERSION=${VERSION}
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Links:
  build system source code: https://github.com/jonaseberle/autoortho-scenery/
  latest release: https://github.com/jonaseberle/autoortho-scenery/releases/
  forum post: https://forums.x-plane.org/forums/topic/346802-autoortho-scenery-flightwusel-packages-for-x-plane-12-as-torrent-downloads/

Installation:
  This does not use the AutoOrtho installer. You need to install it manually.
  You can/should remove the original scenery packages downloaded via the AutoOrtho installer.
  It could be that the installer does not work with it afterwards.
  The original packages are basically not compatible with this because they cover different areas!

  I cannot be held responsible for any problems.

  Please understand first how AutoOrtho works and how you have to set up a new scenery package.
  Many questions are answered in this post:
  https://forums.x-plane.org/forums/topic/303551-when-you-have-a-problem-with-autoortho-%E2%80%93-please-read/
  Please inform yourself and refrain from posting lazy "does not work" posts on the forums unless you have at least
  spent half an hour yourself trying to correct a problem.

  in short:
  * Put the folder into your configured AutoOrtho paths.scenery_path from your AutoOrtho config file
    (by default <X-Plane>/Custom Scenery/z_autoortho/scenery/).
  * Arrange your `scenery_packs.ini`: see the block about it in the mentioned forum post above.


Notice:
  These tiles do not contain the overlay exports! I recommend enjoying them with the simHeaven X-WORLD
  (or X-WORLD PRO) overlays.
  If you do not add overlays, you will NOT see roads, forests, houses, ...!

